                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h2]Somehow this is addictive as it is torturous. No wait, not really.[/h2]\r\n\r\nIf you get this for the achievements, don't! If that's the case, expect to torture yourself for several hours.\r\n\r\nClickdraw Clicker is a clicker game with a twist. It's basically like the old fashioned cup and ball game. The only difference being that you don't get to watch where the ball goes. You guess where the enemy will move to, and also where you will move. So basically, the outcome is you either get hit, you hit your opponent, or you both miss. It gets extremely difficult as time goes on and can feel impossible later in the game. It's 100% dumb luck (AKA RNG). This is basically just a mini game.\r\n\r\nThe game is also not really aesthetically pleasing. It's just got a boring look going for it.\r\n\r\nI do not recommend this game because it's fun... for five minutes. Going for the achievements is not fun at all. I would never play this again for the achievements.\r\n\r\n[h2]3/10[/h2]\r\n\r\n[h3][url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45905648-Gork%2527s-Game-Grind/]Check out my curated list of games[/url][/h3]",
